sd_ass: preserve the complete event-prefetch render state

The shared render-ahead pipeline (osd_ahead) requests isolated event-prefetch
state with OSD_DRAW_PREFETCH. Keep at most
two reusable ASS renderers with their packers so intervening current-frame
renders cannot evict the prepared renderer and atlas. At exact-time promotion,
release only the old renderer's event-layout snapshots through
ass_renderer_clear_layout_cache; retain both renderers' raster/font caches and
worker pools. Render the requested timestamp, including repeated timestamps;
unchanged content reuses the prepared atlas, never an image accepted by age.

Epoch/full-repaint presentation checks remain in the VO. Reset, option changes
and output deselection discard the pending renderer. Other subtitle decoders
accept the render hint without changing behavior. This path does not enable
persistent libass layout caching.

